# awcms-one — root configuration
#
# This file covers variables read by ROOT-LEVEL scripts (packages/gerbang/,
# tools/) only. It is deliberately small: this workspace does not yet have a
# runtime service of its own to configure.
#
#   - apps/cms's own runtime configuration (DATABASE_URL, APP_URL, and the
#     rest of its ~24KB of documented variables) lives in its OWN
#     apps/cms/.env.example, copied to apps/cms/.env. It is a separate
#     deployable with its own database and its own concerns; this file does
#     not duplicate it.
#   - apps/storefront does not exist yet (issue #5). It will need its own
#     env vars — at minimum an origin to reach apps/cms's public API — and
#     they will be documented here, or in its own .env.example, once it
#     lands. Nothing is declared for it now: an unset variable nobody reads
#     yet is a worse kind of documentation than no variable at all.

# Overrides "today" for packages/gerbang/audit-rilis.mjs's changeset-age
# arithmetic. Read as a LOCAL date, `YYYY-MM-DD`.
#
# Not something a contributor normally sets. It exists so the gate's own
# wall-clock logic can be tested against a fixed date instead of the real
# clock — a test that computed its expected dates from the same clock the
# gate reads would only prove that subtraction works, not that the gate
# reads the calendar correctly. Leave this unset for ordinary use; the gate
# then reads the machine's real local date.
# RELEASE_TODAY=2026-09-15

# Overrides the repo root tools/knowledge-graph-combine.mjs and
# tools/knowledge-obsidian-export.mjs operate on (issue #11). Exists so
# tests/knowledge-no-subtree-write.test.mjs can run those tools for real
# against a disposable fixture tree instead of this repo's own apps/cms/ —
# see either tool's own top-of-file comment. Never set this for ordinary
# use; both tools then resolve the real repo root as before.
# KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_ROOT=/path/to/a/fixture/tree
